# CI log:
#   | Test environment jest-environment-jsdom cannot be found. Make sure the testEnvironment configuration option points to an existing node module.
#
# How it is solved:
#   MODIFY jest.config.js
#     - Set testEnvironment to 'node' in jest.config.js — 'jsdom' is not installed (Jest 28+ no longer bundles it) and package.json has no browser/UI dependency, so the tests need no DOM
